<title>ZIMBABWE: Zimbabwe's Wankie half yr shr, div steady.</title>
<headline>Zimbabwe's Wankie half yr shr, div steady.</headline>
<dateline>HARARE 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half-yr ended August 31.</p>
<p>	   (million Zimbabwe dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)			     29 vs 29</p>
<p>    Div (cts)			    7.5 vs 7.5</p>
<p>    Pre-interest profit	     73.3 vs 58.1</p>
<p>    Net interest			 2.0 vs 13.4</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		    75.3 vs 71.5</p>
<p>    Taxation			    27.0 vs 22.6</p>
<p>    After-tax profit		  48.3 vs 48.9</p>
<p>    Sales				358.6 vs 327.3</p>
<p>Div payable November 15</p>
<p>on register October 18.</p>
<p>Full name: Wankie Colliery Company Limited (coal mining)</p>
<p>NOTE: The company said it expected demand for coal to improve in the second half of the year following the completion of refurbishment of the national electricity utility's Hwange Power Station in northern Zimbabwe.</p>
<p>-- Emelia Sithole, Harare Newsroom: +263-4 72 52 27/8/9</p>
</text>
